  "parent": "pt-BR",
  "notes": "Caipira (interior of São Paulo state and the neighbouring areas). Coda /r/ is the retroflex approximant [ɻ] (porta [ˈpoɻtɐ], mar [maɻ]). Amaral (1920) §6b: 'r inter e post-vocálico (arara, carta) possui um valor peculiar: é linguò-palatal e guturalizado'; ALiB: 'o /r/ caipira está presente de forma praticamente categórica em todo o estado de São Paulo [...] exceto na capital e na cidade de Santos' (Silva 2023: 70; Castro 2013: 566). ⟨lh⟩ is [j] (Amaral §25: 'Vocaliza-se em i: [...] muié, fiio'). Coda /l/ is [ɻ] (Amaral §22a: 'Em final de sílaba, muda-se em r: quarqué [...] arma'), with [w] as the second candidate. Amaral also describes intervocalic r as retroflex, ⟨ch j⟩ as affricates (§6d) and final e/o as unraised (§8); the spec does not encode these, because no modern source was opened to confirm them. /t d/ before [i] follow the base: no opened source describes them for this variety.",
  "quality": "research",
  "script_type": "alphabet",
